has no known map position, so the pin is the dungeon entrance."},["an unholy alliance"]={c=S[107],x=1286.5,y=334,w="Undercity",q="An Unholy Alliance",npc="Varimathras (turn-in)",k="giver",note="This quest starts from an item drop in Razorfen Downs; the pin is where you hand it in."}},specs={{id="balance",name="Balance",token="BAL",title="Balance | WoW Forever Druid Field Guide",nav={{id="overview",x=S[727]},{id="journey",x=S[594]},{id="talents",x=S[514]},{id="stats",x=S[622]},{id="combat",x=S[623]},{id="macros",x=S[641]},{id="dungeons",x=S[565]},{id="professions",x=S[595]},{id="crafting",x=S[579]},{id="questgear",x=S[556]},{id=S[507],x=S[671]}},asideNote=S[114],talentString="5032220115501351000000000000000000005253",ranks={{tree="Balance",name=S[688],r=5,max=5},{tree="Balance",name="Moonglow",r=3,max=3},{tree="Balance",name=S[898],r=2,max=2},{tree="Balance",name=S[557],r=2,max=2},{tree="Balance",name=S[689],r=2,max=2},{tree="Balance",name=S[642],r=1,max=1},{tree="Balance",name=S[879],r=1,max=1},{tree="Balance",name="Vengeance",r=5,max=5},{tree="Balance",name=S[899],r=5,max=5},{tree="Balance",name=S[944],r=1,max=1},{tree="Balance",name="Eclipse",r=3,max=3},{tree="Balance",name="Moonfury",r=5,max=5},{tree="Balance",name=S[880],r=1,max=1},{tree="Restoration",name=S[690],r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name=S[535],r=2,max=5,u=true},{tree="Restoration",name="Naturalist",r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name="Reflection",r=3,max=3,u=true}},order={{l1=10,l2=14,tree="Balance",name=S[688],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=15,l2=17,tree="Balance",name="Moonglow",r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=18,l2=19,tree="Balance",name=S[689],r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=20,l2=21,tree="Balance",name=S[557],r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=22,l2=22,tree="Balance",name=S[642],r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=23,l2=24,tree="Balance",name=S[898],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=25,l2=25,tree="Balance",name=S[879],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=26,l2=30,tree="Balance",name="Vengeance",r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=31,l2=31,tree="Balance",name=S[944],r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=32,l2=34,tree="Balance",name="Eclipse",r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=35,l2=39,tree="Balance",name="Moonfury",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=40,l2=40,tree="Balance",name=S[880],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=41,l2=45,tree="Restoration",name=S[690],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=46,l2=48,tree="Restoration",name="Reflection",r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=49,l2=53,tree="Restoration",name="Naturalist",r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=54,l2=58,tree="Balance",name=S[899],r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=59,l2=60,tree="Restoration",name=S[535],r1=1,r2=2,max=5,u=true}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[558]},{t="p",s="legend",x=S[205],u=true},{t="h1",x="Balance",sub=S[643]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Moonfire and Insect Swarm, then Wrath. |cff71d5ffEclipse at 32–34 turns Wrath into faster Starfire casts|r, and Moonkin Form at 40 adds armor and a 3% critical-strike aura for your group."},{t="pills",list={S[772],"Suggested leveling build",S[596]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[728]},{t="h2",x=S[470]},{t="p",x="These stages follow the talent order below. The first levels are slow, and auto-attacking in Bear Form can match Wrath around level 10; leveling speeds up once spell power gear and Insect Swarm arrive."},{t="p",s="level",x="10–25 · Cheaper Wrath, longer reach"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffImproved Wrath 5/5 (10–14) cuts Wrath’s cast time by 0.5 seconds and its mana cost by 50%. Moonglow 3/3 (15–17) makes your spells cheaper, Nature’s Reach 2/2 (18–19) adds 20% range and 4% hit, which helps you tag enemies first in busy zones, Nature’s Majesty 2/2 (20–21) adds 4% critical strike, Nature’s Splendor at 22 lengthens Moonfire, Regrowth and Rejuvenation, then Improved Moonfire 2/2 (23–24) and Insect Swarm at 25.|r"},{t="p",s="level",x="26–40 · Starfire and Moonkin Form"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffVengeance 5/5 (26–30) doubles the critical-strike bonus of your Arcane and Nature spells, and Nature’s Grace at 31 speeds up your next cast after a critical strike. Eclipse 3/3 (32–34) makes each Wrath shorten your next two Starfires by 0.5 seconds (up to four charges); before Eclipse, you can ignore Starfire. Moonfury 5/5 (35–39) adds 10% Arcane and Nature damage, and Moonkin Form arrives at 40.|r"},{t="p",s="level",x="41–60 · Pushback, damage and mana"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffNature’s Focus 5/5 (41–45) protects casts from pushback, Reflection 3/3 (46–48) lets part of your mana regeneration continue while casting, Naturalist 5/5 (49–53) raises all damage by 10%, Improved Starfire 5/5 (54–58) shortens Starfire by 0.5 seconds, and Heart of the Wild 2/5 (59–60) finishes the build.|r"},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[515]},{t="h2",x=S[772]},{t="p",x=S[81],u=true},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[566]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[502]},{t="p",x=S[145],u=true},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="|cff71d5ffMoonkin Form’s critical strike aura does not stack with a Feral Druid’s Leader of the Pack. Moonkin Form prevents healing spells: shift out to cast Rejuvenation or Regrowth.|r"},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[624]},{t="h2",x=S[541]},{t="p",x="Balance wants hit until the cap, then critical strike and spell power. Weapon damage does nothing for your spells."},{t="h3",x=S[691]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[972],x="Nature and Arcane damage count too"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Intellect",x="mana pool"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Spirit",x="faster drinking between pulls"},{t="p",s="small",x="Staves with spell damage and Intellect are your main upgrades while leveling."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b="Hit chance",x="to 17%"},{t="stat",i=2,b=S[928],x=""},{t="stat",i=3,b="Spell power",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Intellect",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Some estimates put spell power above crit, with spell penetration and haste as extras."},{t="p",s="notice",x="Spell hit cap: 17% against raid bosses (level 63), 4% against enemies of your own level. The level 60 list is an early estimate: the beta stopped at level 30, so expect changes once endgame gear is known. A big upgrade in a lower stat can still beat a small one in a higher stat."},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[542]},{t="h2",x=S[580]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority list, not a fixed loop. Insect Swarm arrives at 25, Eclipse at 31, Moonkin Form and Hurricane at 40 in this order."},{t="h4",x=S[929]},{t="p",x="Keep Mark of the Wild and Thorns on yourself, and cast Rejuvenation on yourself before you engage. Open with Moonfire in crowded areas so you tag the enemy instantly, and with Wrath otherwise."},{t="h4",x="Damage over time"},{t="p",x="Keep Moonfire and, from 25, Insect Swarm on enemies that will live long enough for them to tick. Spread both to every enemy in an add pull."},{t="h4",x="Filler"},{t="p",x="Wrath is your filler. With 3/3 Eclipse, cast one Wrath and then two faster Starfires."},{t="h4",x="Staying alive"},{t="p",x="Regrowth mid-fight if you need it; one Rejuvenation and one Regrowth are usually enough. Nature’s Grasp and Entangling Roots keep an extra enemy away; leave Moonkin Form to heal."},{t="h4",x="Several enemies"},{t="p",x="From 40, Hurricane on three or more enemies, ideally with Barkskin so pushback does not cancel it. Before 40, apply your damage over time effects and Wrath one target at a time."},{t="h4",x="Mana"},{t="p",x="Carry several stacks of water and drink after every few enemies. Innervate at 40 restores mana; Omen of Clarity at 20 makes a spell free now and then (Wrath does not consume it)."},{t="abil",names={"Wrath","Moonfire",S[879],"Starfire","Hurricane","Entangling Roots","Nature's Grasp",S[973],"Regrowth",S[880],"Barkskin","Innervate"}},{t="h3",x=S[614]},{t="p",x="Stats for Balance: spell power first, then Intellect, critical strike, haste (rare), Spirit and mana per 5. Weapon damage does not raise your spells."},{t="p",x="Staff path: Golemheart Stave (Hall of Thanes, 13), Emberstone Staff (Deadmines, 17), Crescent Staff (Wailing Caverns quest, 22), Glimmering Staff (Enchanting 140, 25), Illusionary Rod (Scarlet Monastery, 34), Greatstaff of the Necrokhans (Desolace quest, 42) and Radiant Staff (Enchanting 220, 45)."},{t="h3",x=S[543]},{t="p",x=S[74]},{t="p",x=S[109]},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[644]},{t="h2",x=S[455]},{t="p",x=S[76]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[62]},{t="macro",n=S[581],x=S[224],code=S[213]},{t="macro",n=S[625],x=S[230],code=S[232]},{t="macro",n=S[582],x=S[227],code=S[214]},{t="macro",n=S[597],x=S[225],code=S[222]},{t="macro",n=S[615],x=S[231],code=S[258]},{t="macro",n=S[464],x=S[154],code=S[142]},{t="macro",n=S[492],x=S[173],code=S[393]},{t="macro",n=S[583],x=S[223],code=S[255]},{t="macro",n=S[616],x=S[238],code=S[351]},{t="macro",n="Hurricane at your cursor",x="Leaves form and places Hurricane at your cursor without a second click. Learned at 40.",code="#showtooltip Hurricane\n/cancelform\n/cast [@cursor] Hurricane"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Entangling Roots",x="Leaves form and roots the enemy under your pointer or your target. Damage can break the roots.",code="#showtooltip Entangling Roots\n/cancelform\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Entangling Roots"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Moonfire",x="Applies Moonfire to the enemy under your pointer, otherwise your target, so you can spread it in add pulls. Not tested in game.",code="#showtooltip Moonfire\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Moonfire"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Insect Swarm",x="Applies Insect Swarm (talent, 25) to the enemy under your pointer, otherwise your target. Not tested in game.",code="#showtooltip Insect Swarm\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Insect Swarm"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[318]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[672]},{t="h2",x=S[503]},{t="p",x=S[93]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[94]},{t="p",s="notice",x="Balance loot selection · 1 November 2026. Cloth and leather with spell damage, Intellect and Spirit, staves, one-handed maces and daggers with held off-hand items, and caster jewelry. Healing-only bonuses, Fire, Frost, Shadow and Holy bonuses, mail, plate, shields, swords, axes, wands and ranged weapons are left out."},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[544]},{t="h2",x=S[493]},{t="p",x=S[106]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[567]},{t="h2",x=S[471]},{t="p",x="These are items to compare, not a mandatory shopping list. Brackets are 1–9, 10–19, 20–29, 30–39, 40–49, 50–59 and level 60. They use the item’s equip/use requirement, not crafting skill; items with no level requirement are placed by item level. Druids wear cloth and leather and use staves, maces, daggers, fist weapons and polearms (train polearms at a weapon master); this page shows only the pieces that suit Balance. Unknown item requirements remain separate. A published recipe does not establish that its trainer, materials or final acquisition path are available in the beta."},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[545]},{t="h2",x=S[444]},{t="p",x=S[39]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[507]},{t="kicker",x=S[673]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[123]}}},{id="feral-cat",name="Feral (Cat)",token="CAT",title="Feral (Cat) | WoW Forever Druid Field Guide",nav={{id="overview",x=S[727]},{id="journey",x=S[594]},{id="talents",x=S[514]},{id="stats",x=S[622]},{id="combat",x=S[623]},{id="macros",x=S[641]},{id="dungeons",x=S[565]},{id="professions",x=S[595]},{id="crafting",x=S[579]},{id="questgear",x=S[556]},{id=S[507],x=S[671]}},asideNote=S[114],talentString="050022000000000050230302123110124011055",ranks={{tree="Balance",name="Genesis",r=5,max=5},{tree="Balance",name=S[557],r=2,max=2},{tree="Balance",name=S[689],r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name="Ferocity",r=5,max=5},{tree=S[119],name=S[674],r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[634],r=3,max=3,u=true},{tree=S[119],name="Thick Hide",r=3,max=3,u=true},{tree=S[119],name="Savage Fury",r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[759],r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[675],r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[645],r=3,max=3},{tree=S[119],name="Lacerate",r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[830],r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[626],r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[658],r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[729],r=4,max=5},{tree=S[119],name="Primal Bite",r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[804],r=1,max=1},{tree="Restoration",name=S[535],r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name="Naturalist",r=5,max=5,u=true}},order={{l1=10,l2=14,tree=S[119],name="Ferocity",r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=15,l2=17,tree=S[119],name="Thick Hide",r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=18,l2=19,tree=S[119],name=S[674],r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=20,l2=20,tree=S[119],name=S[759],r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=21,l2=22,tree=S[119],name="Savage Fury",r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=23,l2=24,tree=S[119],name=S[675],r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=25,l2=25,tree=S[119],name=S[830],r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=26,l2=26,tree=S[119],name="Lacerate",r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=27,l2=29,tree=S[119],name=S[634],r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=30,l2=30,tree=S[119],name=S[626],r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=31,l2=32,tree=S[119],name=S[658],r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=33,l2=35,tree=S[119],name=S[645],r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=36,l2=39,tree=S[119],name=S[729],r1=1,r2=4,max=5,u=true},{l1=40,l2=40,tree=S[119],name="Primal Bite",r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=41,l2=41,tree=S[119],name=S[804],r1=1,r2=1,max=1,u=true},{l1=42,l2=46,tree="Balance",name="Genesis",r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=47,l2=48,tree="Balance",name=S[689],r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true},{l1=49,l2=53,tree="Restoration",name=S[535],r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=54,l2=58,tree="Restoration",name="Naturalist",r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=59,l2=60,tree="Balance",name=S[557],r1=1,r2=2,max=2,u=true}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[558]},{t="p",s="legend",x=S[205],u=true},{t="h1",x="Feral (Cat)",sub=S[643]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Rake, Claw or Shred and Rip in Cat Form, |cff71d5ffShifting Power to turn mana into Energy at 41,|r and Bear Form whenever a pull gets dangerous. Cat and Bear attacks use your weapon’s damage per second in Forever."},{t="pills",list={S[635],"Open-world leveling build",S[596]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[728]},{t="h2",x=S[470]},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffThese stages follow the talent order below: a Feral DPS build that goes straight down the Feral tree and finishes in Balance and Restoration.|r"},{t="p",s="level",x="|cff71d5ff10–19 · Before Cat Form|r"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffFerocity 5/5 (10–14) makes Claw, Rake, Maul, Swipe and Primal Bite cost 5 less, Thick Hide 3/3 (15–17) adds armor, and Feral Swiftness 2/2 (18–19) adds 30% Cat run speed and 4% dodge. Until Cat Form at 20 you fight with Moonfire, Wrath and Bear Form from 10.|r"},{t="p",s="level",x="|cff71d5ff20–35 · Cat Form core|r"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffFeral Charge at 20, Savage Fury 2/2 (21–22) and Sharpened Claws 2/2 (23–24) come first. Predatory Discipline at 25 lets Ferocious Bite deal extra damage from your excess Energy without spending it, Lacerate at 26 adds a stacking bleed, then Feral Instinct 3/3 (27–29), Leader of the Pack at 30 (3% critical strike for your group in forms), Natural Instinct 2/2 (31–32) and Predatory Strikes 3/3 (33–35).|r"},{t="p",s="level",x="|cff71d5ff36–60 · Bleeds, Primal Bite and Shifting Power|r"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffRend and Tear 4/5 (36–39) adds damage on bleeding targets, Primal Bite arrives at 40, and Shifting Power at 41 converts mana into 40 Energy. Genesis 5/5 (42–46) and Nature’s Reach 2/2 (47–48) come from Balance, then Heart of the Wild 5/5 (49–53), Naturalist 5/5 (54–58) and Nature’s Majesty 2/2 (59–60) finish the build.|r"},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[515]},{t="h2",x=S[635]},{t="p",x=S[81],u=true},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[566]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[502]},{t="p",x=S[145],u=true},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="|cff71d5ffPlay Cat Form solo and Bear Form for dangerous pulls and dungeons. With Predatory Discipline, Ferocious Bite keeps your excess Energy, so you do not need to pool Energy for it.|r"},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[624]},{t="h2",x=S[541]},{t="p",x="Cat Form uses your weapon’s damage per second, so a high-DPS two-hander is your biggest upgrade. Agility and Strength help when weapons are close."},{t="h3",x=S[691]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[730],x="two-handed maces, staves and polearms"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Agility",x="attack power, crit and armor"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Strength",x="attack power"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Weapon speed does not matter: your forms have a fixed attack speed and only the weapon’s damage per second counts."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[730],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Expertise",x="to 6.5%"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Hit chance",x="to 8%"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Agility",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Strength",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Critical strike and attack power are worth about as much as Agility and Strength."},{t="p",s="notice",x="Melee hit cap: 8% for special attacks against raid bosses. Expertise removes dodge at 6.5% and parry at 14% (parry only matters from the front). The level 60 list is an early estimate: the beta stopped at level 30, so expect changes once endgame gear is known. A big upgrade in a lower stat can still beat a small one in a higher stat."},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[542]},{t="h2",x=S[580]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority list, not a fixed loop. Cat Form and Prowl arrive at 20, Rake at 24, Ravage at 32, |cff71d5ffPounce at 36 and Shifting Power (talent) at 41.|r"},{t="h4",x=S[929]},{t="p",x="Keep Mark of the Wild and Thorns active. Open from Prowl with Ravage (32) or Pounce (36) from behind; before that, pull with Moonfire or a free Faerie Fire, which costs nothing in Cat or Bear Form."},{t="h4",x="Bleeds"},{t="p",x="Keep Rake on any target that will live 6 seconds or longer, and a five-combo-point Rip on the same targets. Rend and Tear adds damage against bleeding enemies."},{t="h4",x="Builders"},{t="p",x="Shred when you are behind the enemy or have Clearcasting, otherwise Claw. Pool Energy so Rake and Rip have as little downtime as possible."},{t="h4",x="Finishers"},{t="p",x="Ferocious Bite only when the enemy is about to die (3 seconds or less) and you have more than three combo points."},{t="h4",x="Energy and mana"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffFrom 41, use Shifting Power when no Energy will be wasted, but keep mana for healing.|r"},{t="h4",x="Dangerous pulls"},{t="p",x="Shift to Bear Form for armor and AoE with Swipe; from 44, Barkskin works in forms. Shift out for Regrowth or Healing Touch between enemies."},{t="abil",names={"Cat Form","Prowl","Rake","Claw","Shred","Rip","Ferocious Bite","Ravage",S[804],"Faerie Fire","Dash","Bear Form"}},{t="h3",x=S[614]},{t="p",x="Cat Form attacks use your equipped weapon’s damage per second; the form sets attack speed, so compare weapon DPS first. Use two-handed maces, staves and polearms (polearms can be learned from 20), with Strength and Agility on armor. Hit, critical strike and Stamina help on hard pulls."},{t="p",x="Weapon path: Segmented Spider Leg (Ruins of Lordaeron, 15), Smite’s Mighty Hammer (Deadmines, 18), Graverobber’s Shovel (Stockade, 23), Manual Crowd Pummeler (Gnomeregan, 29), Loksey’s Training Stick (Scarlet Monastery, 31), Grimlok’s Charge (Uldaman, 42), then Thorium Poleaxe (52) and Hammer of the Titans or Legionite Glaive (58) from Blacksmithing."},{t="h3",x=S[543]},{t="p",x=S[74]},{t="p",x=S[109]},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[644]},{t="h2",x=S[455]},{t="p",x=S[76]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[62]},{t="macro",n=S[581],x=S[224],code=S[213]},{t="macro",n=S[625],x=S[230],code=S[232]},{t="macro",n=S[582],x=S[227],code=S[214]},{t="macro",n=S[597],x=S[225],code=S[222]},{t="macro",n=S[615],x=S[231],code=S[258]},{t="macro",n=S[464],x=S[154],code=S[142]},{t="macro",n=S[492],x=S[173],code=S[393]},{t="macro",n=S[583],x=S[223],code=S[255]},{t="macro",n=S[616],x=S[238],code=S[351]},{t="macro",n="Shred, or Shifting Power with Shift",x="Shred in Cat Form; hold Shift to convert mana into Energy with Shifting Power (talent). Shred still needs you behind the enemy.",code="#showtooltip\n/startattack [nomod:shift,harm,nodead]\n/cast [mod:shift] Shifting Power; [harm,nodead] Shred"},{t="macro",n="Dash from Cat Form",x="Enters Cat Form if needed and uses Dash; press again after changing form if it does not fire.",code="#showtooltip Dash\n/cast [noform:3] Cat Form\n/cast Dash"},{t="macro",n=S[792],x="In Cat Form, leaps behind the enemy under your pointer or your target; in Bear Form, charges and interrupts.",code=S[417]},{t="macro",n="Rake with auto-attack",x="Starts auto-attack and applies Rake to your target. Not tested in game.",code="#showtooltip Rake\n/startattack [harm,nodead]\n/cast [harm,nodead] Rake"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[318]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[672]},{t="h2",x=S[503]},{t="p",x=S[93]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[94]},{t="p",s="notice",x="Feral (Cat) loot selection · 1 November 2026. Leather with Strength, Agility, attack power, hit and critical strike, physical jewelry and cloaks, and two-handed maces, staves and polearms (Cat attacks use weapon damage per second). Cloth, caster gear, mail, plate, shields, swords, axes, wands and ranged weapons are left out. Pure Stamina pieces belong to the Tank page."},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[544]},{t="h2",x=S[493]},{t="p",x=S[106]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[567]},{t="h2",x=S[471]},{t="p",x="These are items to compare, not a mandatory shopping list. Brackets are 1–9, 10–19, 20–29, 30–39, 40–49, 50–59 and level 60. They use the item’s equip/use requirement, not crafting skill; items with no level requirement are placed by item level. Druids wear cloth and leather and use staves, maces, daggers, fist weapons and polearms (train polearms at a weapon master); this page shows only the pieces that suit Feral (Cat). Unknown item requirements remain separate. A published recipe does not establish that its trainer, materials or final acquisition path are available in the beta."},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[545]},{t="h2",x=S[444]},{t="p",x=S[39]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[507]},{t="kicker",x=S[673]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[123]}}},{id="feral-tank",name=S[974],token="TANK",title="Feral (Tank) | WoW Forever Druid Field Guide",nav={{id="overview",x=S[727]},{id="journey",x=S[594]},{id="talents",x=S[514]},{id="stats",x=S[622]},{id="combat",x=S[623]},{id="macros",x=S[641]},{id="dungeons",x=S[565]},{id="professions",x=S[595]},{id="crafting",x=S[579]},{id="questgear",x=S[556]},{id=S[507],x=S[671]}},asideNote=S[114],talentString="000000000000000055220302123102115510055",ranks={{tree=S[119],name="Ferocity",r=5,max=5},{tree=S[119],name="Furor",r=5,max=5},{tree=S[119],name=S[674],r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[634],r=2,max=3,u=true},{tree=S[119],name="Thick Hide",r=3,max=3,u=true},{tree=S[119],name="Savage Fury",r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[759],r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[675],r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[645],r=3,max=3},{tree=S[119],name="Lacerate",r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[975],r=2,max=2},{tree=S[119],name=S[626],r=1,max=1},{tree=S[119],name=S[658],r=1,max=2,u=true},{tree=S[119],name=S[729],r=5,max=5},{tree=S[119],name=S[910],r=5,max=5,u=true},{tree=S[119],name="Primal Bite",r=1,max=1},{tree="Restoration",name=S[535],r=5,max=5},{tree="Restoration",name="Naturalist",r=5,max=5}},order={{l1=10,l2=14,tree=S[119],name="Ferocity",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=15,l2=17,tree=S[119],name="Furor",r1=1,r2=3,max=5},{l1=18,l2=19,tree=S[119],name=S[674],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=20,l2=20,tree=S[119],name=S[759],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=21,l2=22,tree=S[119],name="Savage Fury",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=23,l2=24,tree=S[119],name=S[675],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=25,l2=25,tree=S[119],name="Lacerate",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=26,l2=28,tree=S[119],name=S[645],r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=29,l2=29,tree=S[119],name=S[634],r1=1,r2=1,max=3,u=true},{l1=30,l2=30,tree=S[119],name=S[626],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=31,l2=32,tree=S[119],name=S[975],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=33,l2=33,tree=S[119],name=S[658],r1=1,r2=1,max=2,u=true},{l1=34,l2=34,tree=S[119],name=S[634],r1=2,r2=2,max=3,u=true},{l1=35,l2=39,tree=S[119],name=S[729],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=40,l2=40,tree=S[119],name="Primal Bite",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=41,l2=45,tree="Restoration",name=S[535],r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=46,l2=50,tree="Restoration",name="Naturalist",r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=51,l2=52,tree=S[119],name="Furor",r1=4,r2=5,max=5,u=true},{l1=53,l2=55,tree=S[119],name="Thick Hide",r1=1,r2=3,max=3,u=true},{l1=56,l2=60,tree=S[119],name=S[910],r1=1,r2=5,max=5,u=true}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[558]},{t="p",s="legend",x=S[205],u=true},{t="h1",x=S[974],sub=S[643]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Bear Form threat with Maul, Swipe, Lacerate and Primal Bite at 40, and Cat Form for questing between dungeons. Bear attacks use your weapon’s damage per second, and Bear Form multiplies the armor on your gear."},{t="pills",list={S[636],"Tank leveling build",S[596]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[728]},{t="h2",x=S[470]},{t="p",x="These stages follow the talent order below. This tank build takes its extra points in Restoration (“Feral Reflection”), which suits most players better than a Balance alternative."},{t="p",s="level",x="10–24 · Rage, speed and Feral Charge"},{t="p",x="Ferocity 5/5 (10–14) lowers the cost of Maul, Swipe and Primal Bite. Furor 3/5 (15–17) gives Rage when you shift into Bear Form. Feral Swiftness 2/2 (18–19), Feral Charge at 20 to reach and interrupt an enemy in Bear Form, Savage Fury 2/2 (21–22) and Sharpened Claws 2/2 (23–24)."},{t="p",s="level",x="|cff71d5ff25–40 · Lacerate to Primal Bite|r"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffLacerate at 25 is a stacking bleed with high threat. Predatory Strikes 3/3 (26–28), Feral Instinct (29 and 34), Leader of the Pack at 30, Blood Frenzy 2/2 (31–32) for 5 Rage on critical strikes, Natural Instinct at 33, Rend and Tear 5/5 (35–39) and Primal Bite at 40.|r"},{t="p",s="level",x="|cff71d5ff41–60 · Restoration, Rage and armor|r"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffHeart of the Wild 5/5 (41–45) adds 20% Stamina in Bear Form, Naturalist 5/5 (46–50) raises damage, Furor 5/5 (51–52) gives more Rage when you shift into Bear Form, Thick Hide 3/3 (53–55) adds armor, and Natural Reaction 5/5 (56–60) finishes the build.|r"},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[515]},{t="h2",x=S[636]},{t="p",x=S[81],u=true},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[566]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[502]},{t="p",x=S[145],u=true},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="|cff71d5ffLacerate keeps the target bleeding, so Rend and Tear applies to your Bear attacks too. Thick Hide and Natural Reaction come last, once your threat tools are in place, to add armor and mitigation.|r"},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[624]},{t="h2",x=S[541]},{t="p",x="Bear Form multiplies the armor on your gear, so armor and Stamina come first for survival. Your threat comes from damage, so the Cat stats still matter."},{t="h3",x=S[691]},{t="stat",i=1,b="Armor",x="higher-armor leather"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=3,b="Agility",x="dodge and armor"},{t="stat",i=4,b=S[730],x="two-handers"},{t="stat",i=5,b="Strength",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Bear attacks also use your weapon’s damage per second, so keep a strong two-hander."},{t="h3",x="At level 60: survival"},{t="stat",i=1,b="Armor",x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Defense",x="to 440"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Agility",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Dodge",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Bear tanks cannot become immune to crushing blows, so stacking armor and health matters. Armor reduces physical damage by at most 75%."},{t="h3",x="At level 60: threat"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[730],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Expertise",x="to 6.5%, up to 14% when tanking"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Hit chance",x="to 8%"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Agility",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Strength",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Threat follows damage, so a tank with weak gear can lose enemies to strong damage dealers."},{t="p",s="notice",x="Melee hit cap: 8% for special attacks against raid bosses. Expertise removes dodge at 6.5% and parry at 14% (parry only matters from the front). Defense 440 makes a level 63 boss unable to land a critical hit on you. The level 60 list is an early estimate: the beta stopped at level 30, so expect changes once endgame gear is known. A big upgrade in a lower stat can still beat a small one in a higher stat."},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[542]},{t="h2",x=S[580]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority list. Growl arrives at 10, Swipe at 16, Lacerate (talent) at 25, Frenzied Regeneration at 36, Primal Bite and Dire Bear Form at 40 and Barkskin at 44."},{t="h4",x="Pull"},{t="p",x="Cast Faerie Fire to pull from range; it is free in Bear Form. Use Enrage before the pull for extra Rage, and Feral Charge to reach a caster."},{t="h4",x="Hold threat"},{t="p",x="Keep Demoralizing Roar on the enemies you are tanking and use Primal Bite whenever it is ready. Keep Lacerate stacked on your main target."},{t="h4",x="Spend Rage"},{t="p",x="Swipe when fighting several enemies; Maul is your single-target Rage spender. Maul replaces your next auto-attack, so its real Rage cost is higher than listed."},{t="h4",x="Taunts"},{t="p",x="Growl a loose enemy back; Challenging Roar for several. The mouseover macros below taunt without changing target."},{t="h4",x="Survival"},{t="p",x="Barkskin works in forms from 44; Frenzied Regeneration turns Rage into health. Bash interrupts or stops a dangerous enemy."},{t="h4",x=S[945]},{t="p",x="Cat Form becomes more effective for open-world questing, while Bear Form lets you take the tank role whenever you choose."},{t="abil",names={"Bear Form","Maul","Swipe","Lacerate","Primal Bite","Demoralizing Roar","Growl","Challenging Roar","Enrage","Frenzied Regeneration","Bash","Barkskin"}},{t="h3",x=S[614]},{t="p",x="Tanking gear: armor and Stamina first, then Agility for dodge and armor and Defense against critical hits; Strength, attack power and hit add threat. Expertise is extra valuable for tanking. Bear Form multiplies item armor, so higher-armor leather matters."},{t="p",x="Bear attacks also use your weapon’s damage per second, so the two-handed path is the same as Cat’s, preferring Stamina and Agility on the weapon. Ironforge Greathammer (Hall of Thanes quest) and Hammer of Orgrimmar (Ragefire Chasm quest) are the first strong Feral weapons."},{t="h3",x=S[543]},{t="p",x=S[74]},{t="p",x=S[109]},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[644]},{t="h2",x=S[455]},{t="p",x=S[76]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[62]},{t="macro",n=S[581],x=S[224],code=S[213]},{t="macro",n=S[625],x=S[230],code=S[232]},{t="macro",n=S[582],x=S[227],code=S[214]},{t="macro",n=S[597],x=S[225],code=S[222]},{t="macro",n=S[615],x=S[231],code=S[258]},{t="macro",n=S[464],x=S[154],code=S[142]},{t="macro",n=S[492],x=S[173],code=S[393]},{t="macro",n=S[583],x=S[223],code=S[255]},{t="macro",n=S[616],x=S[238],code=S[351]},{t="macro",n="Primal Bite with auto-attack",x="Uses Primal Bite (talent, 40) in Bear or Dire Bear Form and starts auto-attack.",code="#showtooltip Primal Bite\n/startattack [harm,nodead]\n/cast [harm,nodead] Primal Bite"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Lacerate",x="Lacerates the enemy under your pointer or your target, building threat on a second enemy while auto-attack stays on your target.",code="#showtooltip Lacerate\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Lacerate"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Growl",x="Taunts the enemy under your pointer or your target in Bear Form without changing target.",code="#showtooltip Growl\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Growl"},{t="macro",n=S[792],x="Charges the enemy under your pointer or your target in Bear Form, interrupting its cast.",code=S[417]},{t="p",s="small",x=S[318]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[672]},{t="h2",x=S[503]},{t="p",x=S[93]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[94]},{t="p",s="notice",x="Feral (Tank) loot selection · 1 November 2026. Leather, jewelry and cloaks with Stamina, Defense, dodge, bonus armor or Agility, and two-handed maces, staves and polearms with Stamina or physical stats. Pieces with only offensive stats (attack power, hit, critical strike or Strength without Stamina) are on the Cat page instead. Cloth, caster gear, mail, plate and shields are left out."},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[544]},{t="h2",x=S[493]},{t="p",x=S[106]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[567]},{t="h2",x=S[471]},{t="p",x="These are items to compare, not a mandatory shopping list. Brackets are 1–9, 10–19, 20–29, 30–39, 40–49, 50–59 and level 60. They use the item’s equip/use requirement, not crafting skill; items with no level requirement are placed by item level. Druids wear cloth and leather and use staves, maces, daggers, fist weapons and polearms (train polearms at a weapon master); this page shows only the pieces that suit Feral (Tank). Unknown item requirements remain separate. A published recipe does not establish that its trainer, materials or final acquisition path are available in the beta."},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[545]},{t="h2",x=S[444]},{t="p",x=S[39]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[507]},{t="kicker",x=S[673]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[123]}}},{id="restoration",name="Restoration",token="RESTO",title="Restoration | WoW Forever Druid Field Guide",nav={{id="overview",x=S[727]},{id="journey",x=S[594]},{id="talents",x=S[514]},{id="stats",x=S[622]},{id="combat",x=S[623]},{id="macros",x=S[641]},{id="dungeons",x=S[565]},{id="professions",x=S[595]},{id="crafting",x=S[579]}