n",name=S[930],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=59,l2=60,tree="Restoration",name=S[831],r1=1,r2=2,max=2}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[558]},{t="p",s="legend",x=S[205],u=true},{t="h1",x="Restoration",sub=S[643]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Rejuvenation and Regrowth on the tank, Swiftmend at 25 and Wild Growth at 40 for dungeon healing; Moonfire and Wrath when you quest alone."},{t="pills",list={S[773],"Dungeon healing build",S[596]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[728]},{t="h2",x=S[470]},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffThese stages follow the talent order below, a Restoration build for dungeon leveling. Restoration levels slower alone than Feral or Balance.|r"},{t="p",s="level",x="10–25 · Pushback protection and Swiftmend"},{t="p",x="|cff71d5ffNature’s Focus 5/5 (10–14) keeps Healing Touch and Wrath from being pushed back, Naturalist 5/5 (15–19) raises all damage by 10% and shortens Wild Growth’s cast, Bloom at 20 heals when Rejuvenation or Regrowth expires, Gift of Nature 1/5 at 21, Reflection 3/3 (22–24) keeps part of your mana regeneration going while casting, and Swiftmend at 25.|r"},{t="p",s="level",x="26–40 · Healing power and Wild Growth"},{t="p",x="Gift of Nature 5/5 (26–29) for 10% more healing, Nature’s Swiftness at 30 for an instant Nature spell, Living Spirit 3/3 (31–33), Improved Rejuvenation 3/3 (34–36), Improved Regrowth 3/5 (37–39) and Wild Growth at 40, a group heal over seven seconds with a three-second cast."},{t="p",s="level",x="41–60 · Damage, mana and Tranquility"},{t="p",x="Improved Wrath 5/5 (41–45), Moonglow 3/3 (46–48) and Nature’s Majesty 2/2 (49–50) for questing, Nature’s Splendor at 51 for longer heals over time, Improved Regrowth 5/5 (52–53), Tranquil Spirit 5/5 (54–58) for cheaper Healing Touch and Tranquility, and Improved Tranquility 2/2 (59–60)."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[515]},{t="h2",x=S[773]},{t="p",x=S[81],u=true},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[566]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[502]},{t="p",x=S[145],u=true},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="Bloom heals the target for 100% of your Spirit when Rejuvenation or Regrowth runs out, and half as much if it is dispelled, so Spirit has extra value. |cff71d5ffSwiftmend needs your own Rejuvenation or Regrowth on the target and does not consume it.|r"},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[624]},{t="h2",x=S[541]},{t="p",x="Restoration wants healing power first, then mana stats. Bloom heals for part of your Spirit, so Spirit is worth more in this build."},{t="h3",x=S[691]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[972],x="for questing alone"},{t="stat",i=2,b=S[956],x="for dungeons"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Intellect",x="mana pool"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Spirit",x="faster recovery, more Bloom healing"},{t="stat",i=5,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Staves with spell power suit both questing and healing."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[956],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Intellect",x=""},{t="stat",i=3,b="Spirit",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Mana per 5",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b=S[928],x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Some estimates rank critical strike and haste right after healing power. Balance throughput against mana for long fights."},{t="p",s="notice",x="Mana per 5 keeps working while you cast; Spirit regeneration stops for 5 seconds after each spell that costs mana. The level 60 list is an early estimate: the beta stopped at level 30, so expect changes once endgame gear is known. A big upgrade in a lower stat can still beat a small one in a higher stat."},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[542]},{t="h2",x=S[580]},{t="p",x="Healing order for dungeons, then your solo priority. Swiftmend arrives at 25, Nature’s Swiftness at 30, Wild Growth and Innervate at 40."},{t="h4",x="Group buffs"},{t="p",x="Mark of the Wild on the group and Thorns on the tank."},{t="h4",x="Steady healing"},{t="p",x="Keep Rejuvenation on the tank and add it to others as needed; it is mana efficient. Regrowth for stronger targeted healing; Healing Touch only when the tank takes sustained damage."},{t="h4",x="Burst"},{t="p",x="Swiftmend after Rejuvenation for a quick large heal; it is too efficient to save only for emergencies. Nature’s Swiftness gives an instant Healing Touch."},{t="h4",x="Group damage"},{t="p",x="Wild Growth when several party members are hurt and close together; Tranquility for heavy group damage, on a long cooldown."},{t="h4",x="Mana"},{t="p",x="Innervate on cooldown from 40 and drink whenever you can between packs."},{t="h4",x=S[945]},{t="p",x="Rejuvenation on yourself first, then Moonfire and Wrath; Nature’s Grasp or Entangling Roots for an extra enemy, and Hurricane on groups from 40."},{t="abil",names={S[973],"Regrowth","Healing Touch","Swiftmend","Wild Growth",S[708],"Tranquility","Innervate","Remove Curse","Cure Poison","Rebirth","Wrath"}},{t="h3",x=S[614]},{t="p",x="Stats for Restoration while leveling: spell power and healing power first (spell power also speeds up questing), then Intellect, critical strike, haste, Spirit and mana per 5. Spirit also powers Bloom in this build."},{t="p",x="Staves from the Balance path suit healing too when they carry spell power: Golemheart Stave, Crescent Staff, Glimmering Staff and Radiant Staff. Compare a one-hander with a held off-hand item against them."},{t="h3",x=S[543]},{t="p",x=S[74]},{t="p",x=S[109]},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[644]},{t="h2",x=S[455]},{t="p",x=S[76]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[62]},{t="macro",n=S[581],x=S[224],code=S[213]},{t="macro",n=S[625],x=S[230],code=S[232]},{t="macro",n=S[582],x=S[227],code=S[214]},{t="macro",n=S[597],x=S[225],code=S[222]},{t="macro",n=S[615],x=S[231],code=S[258]},{t="macro",n=S[464],x=S[154],code=S[142]},{t="macro",n=S[492],x=S[173],code=S[393]},{t="macro",n=S[583],x=S[223],code=S[255]},{t="macro",n=S[616],x=S[238],code=S[351]},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Swiftmend",x="Leaves form and uses Swiftmend on the ally under your pointer, your friendly target or yourself; they need your Rejuvenation or Regrowth.",code="#showtooltip Swiftmend\n/cancelform\n/cast [@mouseover,help,nodead][help,nodead][@player] Swiftmend"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Wild Growth",x="Leaves form and casts Wild Growth on the ally under your pointer, your friendly target or yourself. In a raid, point at someone in the party you want to heal.",code="#showtooltip Wild Growth\n/cancelform\n/cast [@mouseover,help,nodead][help,nodead][@player] Wild Growth"},{t="macro",n="Nature's Swiftness Healing Touch",x="Stops casting, leaves form and uses Nature’s Swiftness for an instant Healing Touch on the ally under your pointer, your friendly target or yourself.",code="#showtooltip Nature's Swiftness\n/stopcasting\n/cancelform\n/cast Nature's Swiftness\n/cast [@mouseover,help,nodead][help,nodead][@player] Healing Touch"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Healing Touch",x="Leaves form and casts your highest Healing Touch on the ally under your pointer, your friendly target or yourself.",code="#showtooltip Healing Touch\n/cancelform\n/cast [@mouseover,help,nodead][help,nodead][@player] Healing Touch"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[318]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[672]},{t="h2",x=S[503]},{t="p",x=S[93]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[94]},{t="p",s="notice",x="Restoration loot selection · 1 November 2026. Cloth and leather with healing power, Intellect, Spirit and mana per 5, staves, one-handed maces and daggers with held off-hand items, caster jewelry and idols. Fire, Frost, Shadow and Holy damage bonuses, mail, plate, shields, swords, axes, wands and ranged weapons are left out."},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[544]},{t="h2",x=S[493]},{t="p",x=S[106]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[567]},{t="h2",x=S[471]},{t="p",x="These are items to compare, not a mandatory shopping list. Brackets are 1–9, 10–19, 20–29, 30–39, 40–49, 50–59 and level 60. They use the item’s equip/use requirement, not crafting skill; items with no level re