4",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false},{n="Maraudon",lr="46–55",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false},{n="Alcaz Prison",lr="48–53",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false},{n="The Temple of Atal'Hakkar",lr="50–60",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false},{n="Blackrock Depths",lr="52–60",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false},{n="Dire Maul",lr="54–60",st=S[344],no="Not yet confirmed for this beta loot guide. We do not have confirmed dungeon-drop data. Wings: East 54–60, North and West 56–60.",ba=false},{n="Lower Blackrock Spire",lr="55–60",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false},{n="Blackmaw Hold",lr="55–60",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false},{n="Scholomance",lr="58–60",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false},{n="Stratholme",lr="58–60",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false},{n="Shaper’s Terrace",lr="58–60",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false},{n="Upper Blackrock Spire",lr="59–60",st=S[344],no=S[77],ba=false}},professions={{n=S[26],b="Leather armor for every spec: Agility and Strength for Cat and Bear, Intellect and spell power for Balance and Restoration, plus armor kits. It pairs well with Skinning, and early pieces such as Brawler’s Leather Hood are strong upgrades.",camp="Camp Tent gives up to 5% of a level in rested experience once an hour; A must-have after level 30.",cv="The best pieces bind on pickup, so you must craft them yourself. Mail recipes are not usable by a Druid."},{n="Skinning",b="Leather and hides for Leatherworking, or early income for training costs.",camp="Camp Chair adds critical strike chance; The best Feral throughput camping buff before Leader of the Pack.",cv=S[608]},{n="Herbalism",b="Herbs for Alchemy or income. Tauren Druids can also use Cultivation to grow a duplicate herb.",cv=S[608]},{n="Alchemy",b="Healing and mana potions, which work without leaving form in Forever, plus Agility, Strength, Intellect and spell damage elixirs. Pairs well with Herbalism.",cv="Ordinary healing potions are also First Aid crafts in Forever; discolored Alchemy potions have a different effect."},{n="Enchanting",b="Glimmering Staff (140) and Radiant Staff (220), the bind-on-pickup Balance staves for leveling, plus Wizard and Mana Oils, gear enchants and Idol of Swiftness for Restoration.",cv="Pairs with Tailoring for cloth caster gear; avoid expensive enchants on temporary items."},{n="Tailoring",b="Cloth caster armor with spell damage, healing and Intellect for Balance and Restoration, plus bags.",cv="Cloth gives Feral nothing; leather of the same level is usually better for Moonkin Form’s armor bonus."},{n=S[202],b="Two-handed maces and polearms on the Feral weapon path (Heavy Copper Maul, Mithril Warhammer, Thorium Greatmace, Thorium Poleaxe, Hammer of the Titans, Legionite Glaive) and sharpening stones, which work while shapeshifted.",camp="Sharpening Wheel adds Strength.",cv="Plate and mail recipes are of no use to a Druid; you can buy tradable weapons instead."},{n="Engineering",b="Explosives, Target Dummies and trinkets; Highly rated for endgame and PvP.",cv="Many explosives still make you leave Cat or Bear Form. Pairs with Mining."},{n="Mining",b="Ore and stone for Blacksmithing or Engineering, and income; Forever has many more mining nodes and Smelting can be leveled separately.",camp="Lodestone adds melee attack power.",cv="No direct combat bonus beyond the camp effect."},{n="Cooking",b="Buff food adds stats and 5% extra experience from kills while it lasts.",cv="Pick food for your spec: Agility and Strength for Feral, Spirit and Intellect for casters."},{n="First Aid",b="Bandages, healing potions and condition-removal items. First Aid Kit helps survivability.",cv="Your heals are usually faster than bandages; damage interrupts bandaging."},{n="Fishing",b="Fish for Cooking, including buff-food ingredients.",camp="Fish Bowl gives 8% stats; The second-best Feral camping buff.",cv="No guaranteed income is implied."}},gearBrackets={{b="Quest rewards",no="Dungeon quests whose Druid-usable rewards are recorded in the Forever database. Quest rewards carry no level requirement of their own, so each tooltip shows 